---
// Pagina di supporto di Minta. L'app la apre da Impostazioni › Info › Support
// (AppLinks.support nel progetto MintaApp): l'indirizzo app/minta/support/ non
// si cambia senza cambiare anche l'app.
//
// Ogni risposta viene dal codice dell'app o dall'informativa approvata
// (MintaApp/Documentation/INFORMATIVA-PRIVACY-BOZZA.md), verificati il
// 3 ottobre 2026 — non da come l'app "dovrebbe" funzionare. Se l'app cambia
// (lingue, percorsi nelle Impostazioni, regole del credito), si rilegge qui.
//
// Niente indirizzo email in questa pagina: deciso dal proprietario il 3 ottobre
// 2026 (l'eccezione di AGENTS.md vale solo per privacy/). Chi deve scrivere viene
// mandato al recapito che l'app mostra in Impostazioni › Info › Privacy.
// Prima della revisione Apple serve un modo di contatto qui: da decidere.
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { path } from '../../../lib/paths';
---

<Base
  titolo="Minta support | TROVA.ME"
  descrizione="Help with Minta: short answers about recordings, your Minta Cloud account and credit, languages and refunds."
>
  <div class="contenitore">
    <div class="testata">
      <p class="etichetta">Minta</p>
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="apertura">
        Short answers to the questions people ask most about Minta.
      </p>
    </div>


    <section class="sezione">
      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <div class="domande">
        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>Where are my recordings kept?</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              Only on your iPhone. Recordings, transcriptions and summaries stay there until
              you delete them, and they can be included in your iPhone backups if you have
              those switched on. Minta keeps no copy on a server, so I can’t bring back a
              recording you deleted. The details are on the <a href={path('privacy/')}
                >privacy page</a
              >.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>How do I delete my Minta Cloud account? What happens to my credit?</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              In Minta, go to Settings › Minta Cloud account › Delete account, and confirm with
              Apple. Your account and its data on Minta’s server are deleted; your recordings
              stay on your iPhone.
            </p>
            <p>
              Any credit you have left is lost and can’t be recovered, and so are any free
              summaries left from the trial: a new account doesn’t get a new free trial. If you
              only want to stop using Minta Cloud, choose Sign out instead — it keeps your
              account and credit for when you sign in again.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>I paid, but the credit isn’t there.</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              Once Apple has charged you, Minta adds the credit automatically, without charging
              you again. Usually it’s enough to close and reopen Minta. If it says “Sign in
              again to receive your credit”, sign in with Apple and the credit arrives on its
              own. If it still hasn’t arrived after that, get in touch using the contact shown
              in Minta, in Settings › Info › Privacy, and include the date of the purchase.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>What does “Processing on the server…” mean?</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              Your audio or text has reached Minta Cloud and the server is working on it, so it
              can no longer be stopped: it is already being paid for.
            </p>
            <p>
              If iOS interrupts Minta or the connection drops, reopen Minta once you’re online:
              it asks for the same result again, without charging you twice. The server holds
              the result in memory for up to 15 minutes for exactly this, then deletes it. If
              Minta tells you a result was lost and you were charged for it, get in touch using
              the contact shown in Minta, in Settings › Info › Privacy.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>Which languages can Minta transcribe? Does it happen on my iPhone?</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              Sixteen languages: Arabic, Chinese, Dutch, English (US and UK), French, German,
              Hindi, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Portuguese, Russian, Spanish, Swedish
              and Turkish. Choose yours in Settings › Transcription.
            </p>
            <p>
              Transcription happens on your iPhone, with Apple’s speech recognition. If that
              isn’t available for a recording — it depends on the language and on the iPhone —
              Minta asks you, every time, before sending the audio to Apple’s servers. If you
              say no, nothing is sent.
            </p>
            <p>
              With Minta Cloud, after your first credit purchase, you can also choose Minta
              Cloud Whisper: transcription on the server, paid from your credit, and useful in
              noisy rooms or with quiet voices.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="domanda">
          <summary><h3>How do I get a refund?</h3></summary>
          <div class="risposta">
            <p>
              Purchases go through Apple, and so do refunds: ask at <a
                href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a
              >, signed in with your Apple Account. I can’t issue refunds myself.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .testata {
    padding: 48px 0 0;
  }

  .testata h1 {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }


  /* Domande richiuse: da telefono si vede subito l'elenco, e si apre solo
     quella che serve. <details> e' HTML puro, nessun JavaScript. */
  .domande {
    max-width: var(--lettura);
    margin-top: 4px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--bordo);
  }

  .domanda {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bordo);
  }

  .domanda summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 18px 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .domanda summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .domanda summary::after {
    content: '+';
    flex: none;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--accento);
  }

  .domanda[open] summary::after {
    content: '−';
  }

  .domanda h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .risposta {
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .risposta p {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: var(--tenue);
  }

  .risposta p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .testata {
      padding-top: 72px;
    }
  }
</style>
